  "id": "COMPOUND:24290 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (S)-2-Methylbutanoate and HepG2 through a series of target interactions. The compound (S)-2-Methylbutanoate is identified as a target of Raji, a cell line that is itself targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and its metabolite, which in turn targets HepG2. Similarly, (S)-2-Methylbutanoate is also linked to MOVP-3, which targets HepG2 through a different compound. These findings suggest that (S)-2-Methylbutanoate may exert its effects on HepG2 via a pathway involving the targeting of Raji and MOVP-3, which are both implicated in the regulation of HepG2. The evidence supports a mechanism where (S)-2-Methylbutanoate may act as a modulator of cellular processes through the targeting of these intermediates, potentially influencing HepG2 through a complex network of interactions.",
